========================================
PART 1 — SET UP (every PC)
========================================

1. Start

While you are here:

cd C:\Users\username

RUN

git clone https://github.com/Koe458-ui/artz.git
cd artz
git checkout Ored.ai
git log --oneline -1

OUTPUT

The version it will show should match with GitHub Ored.ai last merged version.

---

2. Virtual Environment

RUN

python -m venv C:\Users\username\artz\.venv
C:\Users\username\artz\.venv\Scripts\activate.bat

pip install torch
pip install -r C:\Users\username\artz\ored\model\requirements-dev.txt

---

3. Important

"(.venv)" should be there in front of the command.

It's now:

C:\Users\username\artz\.venv

not:

artz\ored\.venv

From "ored\model", activate with:

RUN

..\..\.venv\Scripts\activate.bat

You should see:

(.venv) C:\Users\username\artz\ored\model>

---

4. Verify CUDA Works

RUN

python -c "import torch; print(torch.cuda.is_available(), torch.cuda.get_device_name(0) if torch.cuda.is_available() else 'No CUDA GPU')"

OUTPUT

True RTX XXXX

Example:

True NVIDIA GeForce RTX 5090

---

5. If CUDA Is False

RUN

pip uninstall -y torch
pip install torch --index-url https://download.pytorch.org/whl/cu128

After successfully running this, check the same CUDA verify code again.

It should display:

True RTX XXXX

---

6. Check the Code Is Sound

RUN

cd C:\Users\username\artz\ored\model
python -m pytest

OUTPUT

xxx passed

The number should be up to date. Check otherwise.

